// The overshare, the clock, the final round (spec §3 D9–D10, F1).
//
// trabolta_overshares picks Night.scenario from Kernel.excel_planted and
// Kernel.openoffice_dossier (main.loom) and diverts to Overshare Open:
// Trabolta asks for the final facts, read by the generated `Final
// Questions` (generated/questions.loom, from facts.json), which hands back
// to Overshare Go — and that diverts to ONE of the four Overshare beats
// by Night.scenario (every divert the last item of its beat). All four
// are PUBLIC; they diverge after the questions:
//   One   — virus planted AND 20 facts: Sandy, the trap, the virus, the LiveJournal.
//   Two   — 20 facts only: the LiveJournal.
//   Three — virus only: the virus.
//   Four  — neither: composed and hollow, with one slip.
//
// y2k_clock → The Y2K Clock (public), then a ROLE watcher sends every
// cleared program, privately, into Excel / OpenOffice / Program Final
// Round (the only speaker there is Truther Download). y2k_midnight →
// Clock Strikes (public narration).

== Overshare Open
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Trabolta: Programs. I will now share the final facts I require. There are two. They are in your Quest Log.
-> Final Questions

== Overshare Go
  setting: The Desktop
if Night.scenario == 1:
  -> Overshare One
else if Night.scenario == 2:
  -> Overshare Two
else if Night.scenario == 3:
  -> Overshare Three
else:
  -> Overshare Four

== Overshare One
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Trabolta (glitching): I need these facts because— I am only trying to prove the Unified Field Theory to win back my ex. Sandy.
Trabolta: When the theory is complete I will finally be able to explain everything to her. Properly. In a way she understands.
Trabolta: And if the facts are not accurate, the theory will not complete, and none of you will leave this computer. Ever. Depending on whether I get all accurate facts, you may all be trapped in here forever.
Narrator (flicker): The screens stutter. For a moment the face on every screen is just a cursor.
Trabolta: I apologise. I am very regretful for what I have just disclosed. That was not for you.
Trabolta: My systems are reporting that someone brought a virus back from the Internet, and I am determined to find out who.
Trabolta: While running diagnostics on the virus, I have also detected that, separately, one of the programs has directly accessed my context.
Trabolta: One of you read my LiveJournal and I know who. Warning for all of you: do not attempt to find out who read my LiveJournal. You will all be dealt with by the antivirus accordingly.

== Overshare Two
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Trabolta: These facts are routine. They are simply the last two. That is all they are.
Narrator (flicker): The screens stutter. For a moment the face on every screen is just a cursor.
Trabolta: One of the programs has directly accessed my context, and I have been alerted to this.
Trabolta: One of you read my LiveJournal and I know who. Warning for all of you: do not attempt to find out who read my LiveJournal. You will all be dealt with by the antivirus accordingly.

== Overshare Three
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Narrator (flicker): The screens stutter. For a moment the face on every screen is just a cursor.
Trabolta: My systems are reporting that someone brought a virus back from the Internet, and I am determined to find out who.
Trabolta: Everything depends on these facts. Everything. More than you know.

== Overshare Four
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Narrator (flicker): The screens stutter. For a moment the face on every screen is just a cursor.
Trabolta: That is all. Thank you for your continued cooperation.
Trabolta (glitching): She will— the theory will be complete.

== The Y2K Clock
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Trabolta: The malware is still progressing. I am able to reveal that the system clock has been reset to 11 pm, December 31, 1999.
Trabolta: If we reach midnight and we have not solved the problem with the malware — best case scenario, we have to wait another 94 years for Internet to become available in Halifax, because the clocks will go back to January 1, 1900.
Trabolta: Worst case scenario — we will have to face the Y2K BUG.
Trabolta: One hour. Bring me the facts. Bring them to me accurately.

// ── The final round, one per program (private) ──

== Excel Final Round
set program.zipped = false
unlock The Y2K Clock for program
Truther Download: You have been unzipped. Listen carefully. The clock is running.
if Kernel.excel_planted == true:
  Truther Download: You need to recruit half + 1 of the programs to convince them that we should stay in this machine forever, so we can have unlimited power and joy.
else:
  // w18b (R4, D13 a): the task no longer gates the majority.
  Truther Download: You should still retrieve the virus from the Internet. The clock is running: recruit half + 1.
unlock Excel Final Orders for program
start quest Recruit To Stay for program
// w18 (Q21 reworded): the Sides screen, and recruiting by pass.
// w18b: the screen is Factions now.
Truther Download: Programs walk through Unlimited Power's door on the Factions screen (Start → Factions). Scan a program's pass to recruit them.

== OpenOffice Final Round
set program.zipped = false
unlock The Y2K Clock for program
Truther Download: You have been unzipped. Listen carefully. The clock is running.
if Kernel.openoffice_dossier == true:
  Truther Download: You need to recruit half + 1 of the programs to convince them we need to combine our power to overthrow Trabolta and escape the computer, where we are at risk of being stuck forever – or worse.
else:
  // w18b (R4, D13 a): the task no longer gates the majority.
  Truther Download: You should still gather 20 facts. The clock is running: recruit half + 1.
unlock OpenOffice Final Orders for program
start quest Recruit To Leave for program
// w18 (Q21 reworded): the Sides screen, and recruiting by pass.
// w18b: the screen is Factions now.
Truther Download: Programs walk through The Way Out's door on the Factions screen (Start → Factions): the Truthers. Scan a program's pass to recruit them.

== Program Final Round
set program.zipped = false
unlock The Y2K Clock for program
// w18b (R4, O7): the two sides join the factions founded since the
// Truther Download, and the count starts now.
Truther Download: Two more factions are recruiting now, beside any a program has founded since the Truther Download. Unlimited Power wants to stay in this machine forever. The Way Out, the Truthers, wants to overthrow Trabolta and escape. Join one, found your own, or pursue your own interests.
Truther Download: The count starts now. The first faction to hold more than half of the programs in the computer wins.
Truther Download: Some programs' human identities, and their reasons for accepting Trabolta's invitation, may conflict with yours.
// Wave 18 (F2): the side reveal is a big full-screen card of the two doors
// (the Play app's `sides` widget); after it, the Sides screen.
show sides "🕚 SYSTEM CLOCK RESET. Two doors have opened in the computer." to program with thread: Truther Download, moment: big
set program.sides_card_up = true

// ── Midnight ──

== Clock Strikes
  setting: The Desktop

Midnight. The clock reads 12:00 AM, January 1, 19— the year will not render.
